      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Meteorites fall from the sky and leave craters of meteorite blocks. Shred them into §6Meteorite Powder§r and smelt it with cobalt in the Blast Furnace to get §6Meteorite Ingots§r - the material behind starmetal and decorated cobalt tools.\n\nMeteorite ingots come out hot. On a desh anvil, two hot ingots are smithed into a §6Forged Meteorite Ingot§r, and two hot forged ingots into a §6Meteorite Blade§r.\n\nMeteors strike at random near players on the Overworld, and now and then a §emeteor shower§r makes them twenty times as frequent. A rare one comes down as solid meteorite or a ball of ores. A §6Charm of Protection§r in your armor (or on a pedestal within 100 blocks) steers them away and stops them from breaking blocks; a §6Meteor Charm§r, made with a volcanic gem, stops them from falling near you at all - and your meteorite supply with them.",
